# Example EnvironmentFile for contrib/systemd/pyck-debug-worker@.service.
#
# RHEL convention: /etc/sysconfig/pyck-debug-worker (Debian uses /etc/default
# instead). Install at that path, mode 0600, owned by root:
#
#   sudo install -m 0600 pyck-debug-worker.sysconfig.example \
#     /etc/sysconfig/pyck-debug-worker
#
# All variables are optional — absent credentials simply gate off the
# temporal/namespace/longpoll and auth/tenant stages (see README). Never put
# a credential on the command line; the binary itself refuses that.

# One of these three selects the pyck service/user token (first match wins).
#PYCK_API_TOKEN=
#PYCK_SERVICE_TOKEN=
#PYCK_AUTH=

# Enables the temporal/namespace stages (+ longpoll, always on by default).
#TEMPORAL_API_KEY=

# Cross-checked against the resolved tenant id; a mismatch is a FAIL.
#PYCK_API_TENANT_ID=
#TEMPORAL_NAMESPACE=

# Overrides the GraphQL gateway used for the auth/tenant stages.
#PYCK_GATEWAY_URL=
